      reports "exists" when the vault is already populated, preserving
      idempotency.
    - A coding-playbook hub template is planned as its own InitStep
      when the vault is new. The template contains the exact section
      structure (Task Routing table, How to Use This Index, Always
      Read First, Sections, Contents) so the study-playbook skill's
      crawling protocol works on day one. Sections are structurally
      present but content-empty.
    - A vault-root CLAUDE.md is planned as its own InitStep when the
      vault is new. It contains wikilink crawling protocol, decision
      protocol (coding conventions vs. search_notes), a "where to find
      things" table, and the brain's role in AIDE — enough for any
      agent reading the vault to know how to navigate it without prior
      knowledge.
    - The Obsidian MCP server prescription is planned with the correct
      platform-aware command (cmd /c wrapper on Windows, direct npx
      otherwise), and reports "exists" when the obsidian key is
      already present in the MCP config.
    - Every InitStep returned is a planning artifact only — no files
      are written to disk by this helper. The calling agent or
      applySteps orchestrator handles all writes.
